    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22655" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incūrĭa</span></b> , ae,
			f.
		2. in - cura, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>want of care</i>, <i>carelessness</i>, <i>negligence</i>, <i>neglect</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">milites populi R. incuriā, fame,
					morbo, vastitate consumpti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Prov. Cons. 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">magistratuum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					3, 31</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">eorum comperta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 4, 48</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vel tolerantia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Agr.
					20</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rei maxime necessariae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Lael. 23, 86</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">maculae quas aut incuria fudit Aut, etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. A.
					P. 352</span></i>
			: capilli, Tert. Poen. <i>ext.</i></div>
